        "title": "Hosting backend mode flips from convex to shadow",
        "summary": "The `HOSTING_BACKEND` constant in `common/src/constants/hosting-backend.ts` changes from 'convex' to 'shadow' to activate the shadow-read mode of the hosting Postgres migration. In this mode, Convex continues to serve all hosting reads and writes, while server paths additionally read the Postgres copy maintained by the `hosting.projection` chain. The change enables logging of `convex_pg_shadow_row_mismatch` with column names only to verify consistency between the stores before fully switching to Postgres.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/constants/hosting-backend.ts`, the export constant `HOSTING_BACKEND` value changed from 'convex' to 'shadow'.",
